+This page defines amplitude amplification for a supplied measurement-free unitary and orthogonal success projection. It fixes the sign and order of the standard iterate, treats zero and unit success weights without normalizing a zero component, and keeps conditional quantum outputs distinct from classical verified outputs. The page proves the rotation formula, known and unknown success procedures with their query costs, an exact-success construction under explicit coherent flag, exact-rotation, and enlarged-zero-reflection access (directly supplied or constructed from controlled original zero reflection), and Høyer’s arbitrary-phase matching and mismatch bounds. The enlarged good reflection is constructed and charged by flag compute–phase–uncompute or explicitly supplied; the terminal projective instrument is separately supplied or constructed with its additional calls. Preparation, inverse access, phase operations, controlled access, verification, gate synthesis, and classical costs remain separately declared.
